# Cyclomatic complexity

## Requirement

- Cyclomatic complexity (McCabe) MUST be measured for supported languages at method/function level wherever the analyzer supports this granularity.
- The corporate reference threshold is **10 (approved maximum per function/method)**, a binding QA limit where the configured analyzer supports function-level results.
- Applicable language-specific rules MUST document the analyzer, counting conventions, thresholds and evidence.
- QA decisions MUST be based on agreed thresholds and documented exceptions, not merely a project-wide sum.

## Verification

Keep analysis reports outside the release product. IASI owns the policy; analyzers such as SonarQube produce the evidence.
